# Built binaries. Each service compiles to one at the repo root, so a plain
# `go build ./services/...` leaves them in the working tree.
#
# Every service binary is named sr or sr-<service>, so a pattern covers them
# all, including one added later. A per-binary list went stale twice: sr-agent,
# and then sr-eval, were built and unlisted, and sr-eval got committed. Anchored
# at the root, so services/sr-*/ itself is untouched.
/sr
/sr-*

# A service built in place (`go build` inside services/<name>/) leaves its binary
# beside the source; unanchored on purpose, so it is caught at any depth.
services/*/sr-*

# Where `make build` puts the same binaries. The entries above cover a bare
# `go build ./services/...`, which drops them at the root; the Makefile builds
# with -o bin/ instead, so both layouts have to be listed or whichever one is
# not gets committed.
/bin/

# Where `make mock` installs the pinned a10n-claude-mock the e2e suites drive.
/.bin/

# Where the e2e harness builds the binary it drives. Under the git directory
# rather than the system temp dir, because macOS reaps /var/folders mid-run —
# see tests/e2e/harness/harness.go. Listed here for the case where someone
# points it at the tree instead.
/.e2e-bin/

# The session state store, and the sidecars SQLite keeps beside an open one.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Agent worktrees. Claude Code puts an isolated sub-agent's checkout here, which
# is a whole second copy of this repository — so a tool that walks the tree
# (gofmt, go vet, a CI lint step) sees every file twice and reports the copy's
# path as though it were ours.
/.claude/worktrees/

# The authoring guides are generated from the authoring-guardrails skill by
# tools/skilldocs at docs-site build time (website: scripts/pull-docs.mjs), so the
# skill is the only copy in this repo. A local preview run lands here.
/docs/guides/
